WEBVTT

00:01:49.176 --> 00:01:54.045
Thank you very much
for being with us today.

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:56.674
Attention, please,
all passengers.

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:59.651
We will shortly be landing
in St. Lowel...

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:02.153
the largest city on Mars.

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:04.622
Today's temperature is a cool
11 degrees Celsius.

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:06.750
The oxygen percentage
reading is 7%.

00:02:06.827 --> 00:02:08.260
Due to public
demonstrations...

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:11.456
there is a slight unrest
throughout the city today.

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:12.964
As a precaution...

00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:15.467
we recommend using our
spaceport shuttle service...

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:16.968
for your safety.

00:02:17.037 --> 00:02:19.437
Thank you.

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:22.066
C'mon, Kelly.

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:24.667
You can't act
like you do on Earth.

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:26.974
We've got a concert schedule
to keep.

00:02:27.047 --> 00:02:28.981
I really need some rest.

00:02:29.049 --> 00:02:31.108
I don't want to perform
for people now.

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:33.414
Why are you acting
so selfish now?

00:02:33.487 --> 00:02:36.320
I hope my guitar
is all right.

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:39.790
We've paid big bucks for a whole
block of the cargo room.

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:42.761
They're treating your guitar
like a national treasure.

00:02:54.875 --> 00:02:59.938
Ladies and gentlemen,
we've just landed now.

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:01.446
Please remain seated...

00:03:01.515 --> 00:03:03.949
and keep your seat belts
fastened...

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:06.349
until we come
to a full stop.

00:03:48.595 --> 00:03:50.085
Huh? The cargo room?

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:53.963
What's going on?
- What's happening?

00:04:33.707 --> 00:04:35.504
Western movie?

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:44.576
Hey!

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:51.889
Freeze!

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:53.323
Get your hands up!

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:58.056
I said get
your hands up now!

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:04.066
Hey, what's up?

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:06.128
Stay back,
Detective Sylibus.

00:05:06.206 --> 00:05:08.071
Who are you?

00:05:10.644 --> 00:05:12.077
Get back!

00:05:26.526 --> 00:05:28.721
You packin' a gun,
cowboy?

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:32.620
Oh, shit.

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:34.997
Cowboys up the ass,
and nobody's got a gun.

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:40.172
Stop!

00:05:51.418 --> 00:05:53.283
I'm falling!

00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:55.184
Look, the bastard's
getting away!

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.497
Don't do it!

00:06:05.565 --> 00:06:06.827
Detective Sylibus...

00:06:08.735 --> 00:06:11.203
the MPD...

00:06:11.271 --> 00:06:13.796
welcomes you...

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:15.465
to your new post.

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:36.260
It's Kelly! She's dead!

00:06:42.702 --> 00:06:43.862
Kelly?

00:06:48.808 --> 00:06:50.435
How could he do that?

00:07:18.538 --> 00:07:19.903
Damn it!

00:07:28.348 --> 00:07:29.781
Hey! Wait!

00:07:34.821 --> 00:07:36.152
This is insane.

00:07:39.159 --> 00:07:41.684
Are you all right?

00:07:57.844 --> 00:08:00.677
Her name was Kelly McCanon.

00:08:00.747 --> 00:08:06.208
I guess country singers
are extinct in the universe now.

00:08:06.286 --> 00:08:07.617
And the suspect?

00:08:09.222 --> 00:08:13.625
Is that getup you're wearing
standard-issue MPD uniform?

00:08:13.693 --> 00:08:15.593
Of course not.

00:08:15.662 --> 00:08:17.960
What's your name?

00:08:18.031 --> 00:08:20.864
Armitage.

00:08:20.934 --> 00:08:22.868
What broad shoulders.

00:08:22.936 --> 00:08:24.836
I love hunks like you.

00:08:26.639 --> 00:08:28.800
What's that for?
I was just being nice.

00:08:28.875 --> 00:08:29.807
Hey!

00:08:29.876 --> 00:08:32.276
Is this somebody's idea
of a sick joke?

00:08:32.345 --> 00:08:34.870
The country star
wasn't even human.

00:08:39.752 --> 00:08:41.720
It's a robot!

00:08:45.592 --> 00:08:46.559
What's wrong?

00:08:49.095 --> 00:08:50.892
What is this?

00:08:52.198 --> 00:08:55.998
Airport police.
This is their jurisdiction.

00:09:07.914 --> 00:09:10.178
Look! They're here!

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:13.151
Get the camera over there!
Hurry up!

00:09:13.219 --> 00:09:14.652
Are you with MPD?

00:09:14.721 --> 00:09:16.586
I'm with Mars Broadcasting!

00:09:16.656 --> 00:09:18.624
We've heard a rumor that
the murdered Kelly McCanon...

00:09:18.691 --> 00:09:20.955
was actually a robot.

00:09:21.027 --> 00:09:22.016
Is this true?

00:09:22.095 --> 00:09:24.325
There are conflicting
reports.

00:09:25.565 --> 00:09:28.261
No comment.

00:09:28.334 --> 00:09:30.768
Well, I'm reporting
from the front...

00:09:30.837 --> 00:09:33.237
of the Martian
Police Department.

00:09:33.306 --> 00:09:36.275
An officer from the scene
is here now.

00:09:36.342 --> 00:09:39.277
He has not, however,
given any official comment...

00:09:39.345 --> 00:09:41.677
nor has
the Police Department.

00:09:45.785 --> 00:09:48.777
Well...

00:09:48.855 --> 00:09:51.380
the question is,
what do we have here?

00:09:51.457 --> 00:09:54.722
Let me report the result from
my preliminary examination...

00:09:54.794 --> 00:09:59.561
and... well... uh...

00:09:59.632 --> 00:10:02.533
the, uh, victim,
shall we call her...

00:10:02.602 --> 00:10:06.231
is neither human
nor cyborg.

00:10:06.306 --> 00:10:08.206
I concluded
that she was a robot.

00:10:08.274 --> 00:10:13.906
Human body tissue can be
replaced by organic material...

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:17.108
but the brain cannot.

00:10:17.183 --> 00:10:20.118
The victim's brain is absolutely
artificial intelligence...

00:10:20.186 --> 00:10:21.483
a computer.

00:10:21.554 --> 00:10:24.955
Her physical construction
was created organically...

00:10:25.024 --> 00:10:26.457
but it was done...

00:10:26.526 --> 00:10:27.959
using a technology
much more advanced...

00:10:28.027 --> 00:10:31.394
than the current
Second Series models.

00:10:31.464 --> 00:10:32.396
Therefore...

00:10:32.465 --> 00:10:34.399
this... well...

00:10:34.467 --> 00:10:35.456
the victim...

00:10:35.535 --> 00:10:39.631
was built illegally,
outside of regulations.

00:10:39.706 --> 00:10:40.638
Thank you.

00:10:40.707 --> 00:10:42.140
Now,
Detective Sylibus...

00:10:42.208 --> 00:10:45.143
would you describe
the crime scene?

00:10:48.348 --> 00:10:51.749
Uh... I'm Ross Sylibus
from Chicago.

00:10:57.023 --> 00:10:59.821
The suspect seemed
like he wanted...

00:10:59.892 --> 00:11:05.125
to transport the body
without anyone noticing...

00:11:05.198 --> 00:11:08.167
probably to finish his work
somewhere else in private.

00:11:08.234 --> 00:11:11.670
But because Officer Armitage had
been trailing the suspects...

00:11:11.738 --> 00:11:13.103
all hell broke loose.

00:11:13.172 --> 00:11:15.868
Armitage,
can you fill us in?

00:11:15.942 --> 00:11:16.874
Yes.

00:11:16.943 --> 00:11:20.344
I just saw that
they were armed.

00:11:20.413 --> 00:11:23.314
I didn't think they were
carrying a dead robot.

00:11:23.383 --> 00:11:25.647
So what does that mean?

00:11:25.718 --> 00:11:28.050
That McCanon's impostor
was riding the shuttle?

00:11:28.121 --> 00:11:29.986
Shut up, Eddie.

00:11:30.056 --> 00:11:32.820
What did her manager
have to say?

00:11:32.892 --> 00:11:37.795
Well, sir, he said
the woman he sat with...

00:11:37.864 --> 00:11:39.297
was the real McCanon.

00:11:39.365 --> 00:11:43.165
And nobody saw her come out
of the terminal.

00:11:43.236 --> 00:11:47.229
The only suspicious passenger
he saw was Detective Sylibus.

00:11:47.306 --> 00:11:50.833
Where is
the real McCanon then?

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:53.344
Maybe she got
tired of working.

00:11:53.413 --> 00:11:57.042
Mighta found herself
a lover-boy.

00:11:57.116 --> 00:11:59.277
Zip it, Eddie!

00:11:59.352 --> 00:12:01.252
How was she acting
inside the shuttle?

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:02.412
Just fine.

00:12:02.488 --> 00:12:04.752
She was holding
a normal conversation.

00:12:04.824 --> 00:12:07.691
If that was a robot...

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:10.729
I doubt if she's ever
been a human.

00:12:13.833 --> 00:12:17.200
Are you telling us
that this robot was really her?

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:20.967
You think that prima donna was
a machine from the beginning?

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:22.166
No.

00:12:22.241 --> 00:12:25.608
I'm saying you can't
distinguish it from a human.

00:12:25.678 --> 00:12:28.545
Oh, Armitage...

00:12:28.614 --> 00:12:32.277
when you realized that
the corpse was a robot...

00:12:32.351 --> 00:12:34.182
you were very shocked.

00:12:34.253 --> 00:12:36.346
Did you notice something?

00:12:36.422 --> 00:12:37.719
Not really.

00:13:04.517 --> 00:13:06.644
Wow.

00:13:06.719 --> 00:13:09.688
The sky is beautiful.

00:13:12.892 --> 00:13:14.257
Twelfth floor.

00:13:23.002 --> 00:13:24.731
It smells stale.

00:13:24.804 --> 00:13:26.795
Is that all your luggage?

00:13:26.873 --> 00:13:30.502
Well, with all the excitement
at baggage claim today...

00:13:30.576 --> 00:13:33.067
just as well.

00:13:33.146 --> 00:13:35.478
Probably stuff
I wouldn't need anyway.

00:13:35.548 --> 00:13:38.483
There's enough trash
from Earth here already.

00:13:38.551 --> 00:13:40.348
You have a point.

00:13:42.755 --> 00:13:43.983
It's her.

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:50.022
This is a tape
sent by the suspect...

00:13:50.096 --> 00:13:52.860
in yesterday's
St. Lowel spaceport shooting.

00:13:59.172 --> 00:14:00.662
What is this?

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:02.469
Is it a memorial program?

00:14:13.352 --> 00:14:15.286
The following scenes
contain graphic content...

00:14:15.354 --> 00:14:17.515
and viewer discretion
is advised.

00:14:17.590 --> 00:14:22.391
If you have children,
please set your monitor to L.

00:14:22.461 --> 00:14:23.655
That's the guy.

00:14:29.635 --> 00:14:32.763
I'll go ahead
and pick up the baggage.

00:14:36.909 --> 00:14:38.570
Who are you?

00:14:47.286 --> 00:14:49.584
Help me... please.

00:15:07.974 --> 00:15:09.942
Please stop.

00:15:10.009 --> 00:15:12.341
Why... why me...

00:15:14.447 --> 00:15:16.005
My god!

00:15:20.586 --> 00:15:22.417
Jessica!

00:15:46.379 --> 00:15:50.008
And there it is
in all its brutal detail.

00:15:53.953 --> 00:15:56.513
To discuss the videotape
we just watched...

00:15:56.589 --> 00:15:59.251
we have with us
in the studio today...

00:15:59.325 --> 00:16:01.020
famous Neo-humanist
activist...

00:16:01.093 --> 00:16:02.754
Julia Blanshin.

00:16:02.828 --> 00:16:04.261
What do you think?

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:09.927
Well... what I am going to say
may surprise most viewers.

00:16:10.002 --> 00:16:16.601
Our goal is to eliminate
all robots from our society.

00:16:16.676 --> 00:16:19.440
The same goal as the suspect
may have had?

00:16:19.512 --> 00:16:24.279
But we don't believe
the problem can be solved...

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:25.817
with street violence.

00:16:43.436 --> 00:16:44.460
Jennifer!

00:16:48.975 --> 00:16:52.308
Hey! Hold on! Hey!

00:16:56.215 --> 00:16:58.445
Shit!

00:17:13.232 --> 00:17:15.496
You pile of shit!

00:17:15.568 --> 00:17:17.433
C'mon! C'mon!

00:17:17.503 --> 00:17:19.300
You fucker!

00:18:36.582 --> 00:18:38.174
Amazing.

00:18:38.250 --> 00:18:42.277
They think they can build
this kind of stuff anywhere.

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:55.061
You're here pretty early,
Sylibus.

00:18:55.134 --> 00:18:56.499
She's gone already...

00:18:56.569 --> 00:18:59.470
the badge-toting terror
in hot pants.

00:19:02.942 --> 00:19:05.206
This time, don't kill...

00:19:05.277 --> 00:19:07.438
your partner.

00:19:14.053 --> 00:19:16.453
Let me tell you something.

00:19:16.522 --> 00:19:20.390
When she puts
on her visor, then...

00:19:20.459 --> 00:19:21.858
watch out.

00:19:21.927 --> 00:19:23.861
Here.

00:19:23.929 --> 00:19:26.295
Your car is waiting
downstairs.

00:19:26.365 --> 00:19:29.493
Welcome to Mars.

00:19:38.444 --> 00:19:40.435
Oh, it's a Ferrari!

00:19:40.513 --> 00:19:42.447
This is too cool!

00:19:49.855 --> 00:19:51.447
Is this manual drive?

00:19:51.524 --> 00:19:54.118
Nope. It has robot-drive
capability...

00:19:54.193 --> 00:19:56.252
but I drive it myself.

00:19:58.998 --> 00:20:01.330
Actually,
I don't trust machines.

00:20:06.038 --> 00:20:07.471
Sounds cool.

00:20:07.540 --> 00:20:11.340
You know, the Lieutenant
just bought a new car.

00:20:11.410 --> 00:20:12.843
Before he got rid
of the old car...

00:20:12.912 --> 00:20:15.847
he realized that he'd never
driven it by himself before.

00:20:15.915 --> 00:20:18.850
I tried to stop him
before he took it out...

00:20:18.918 --> 00:20:20.852
'cause it's dangerous,
don't you think?

00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:22.683
I mean, someone who's
never before...

00:20:37.836 --> 00:20:40.236
Robots get out!

00:20:40.306 --> 00:20:43.207
Robots get out!

00:20:43.275 --> 00:20:45.140
Get out right now!

00:20:45.211 --> 00:20:47.907
Get out right now!

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:51.882
Give us back our jobs!

00:20:51.951 --> 00:20:55.443
Give us back our jobs!

00:20:58.424 --> 00:21:00.949
I'm sorry to break you
in so soon...

00:21:01.026 --> 00:21:03.722
but we may as well
get started.

00:21:03.796 --> 00:21:08.256
But, Lieutenant, is our section
supposed to handle this matter?

00:21:08.334 --> 00:21:11.235
What do you mean by that?

00:21:11.303 --> 00:21:14.431
The victim was definitely
a robot...

00:21:14.506 --> 00:21:17.441
but this is not
within our jurisdiction...

00:21:17.509 --> 00:21:19.636
I mean, robot crimes.

00:21:19.712 --> 00:21:22.203
As a rule,
you may be right...

00:21:22.281 --> 00:21:24.215
but it's the illegal
robot's origins...

00:21:24.283 --> 00:21:26.717
that we are interested
in finding out.

00:21:26.785 --> 00:21:28.980
Besides, can't you tell
this case is not simply...

00:21:29.054 --> 00:21:30.783
a property damage charge?

00:21:30.856 --> 00:21:32.517
Yes, sir, but...

00:21:32.591 --> 00:21:35.890
Are you going to tell me why
you want a transfer to Mars?

00:21:35.961 --> 00:21:37.394
N-no, sir.

00:21:37.463 --> 00:21:40.398
If you have misguided
compassion for robots...

00:21:40.466 --> 00:21:42.457
you won't make it here.

00:21:47.973 --> 00:21:50.032
Robots get out!

00:21:50.109 --> 00:21:53.010
Robots get out!

00:21:53.078 --> 00:21:55.546
Get out right now!

00:22:15.768 --> 00:22:17.827
Isn't it winter?

00:22:19.905 --> 00:22:21.839
Did you watch the news?

00:22:21.907 --> 00:22:23.841
This is a photo of the corpse.

00:22:23.909 --> 00:22:26.241
It's being called
a Third Series robot.

00:22:26.312 --> 00:22:29.907
Yes, this is
an elaborate product.

00:22:29.982 --> 00:22:32.416
Certainly not mass produced.

00:22:32.484 --> 00:22:35.715
I guess they used
specialized parts.

00:22:35.788 --> 00:22:38.222
Do you have
any robots like this?

00:22:38.290 --> 00:22:42.249
This is not the type of robot
that Hu-Gite manufactures.

00:22:42.328 --> 00:22:44.228
We surpassed
the Conception company...

00:22:44.296 --> 00:22:47.561
and became the best
because of our philosophy.

00:22:47.633 --> 00:22:49.658
Are you familiar with it?

00:22:53.572 --> 00:22:55.631
Home robotization...

00:22:55.708 --> 00:22:58.199
making the robot
a part of the family...

00:22:58.277 --> 00:23:00.211
by making it more functional.

00:23:00.279 --> 00:23:03.544
A humanoid robot
simply doesn't work.

00:23:03.615 --> 00:23:06.049
There has to be a reason
and purpose...

00:23:06.118 --> 00:23:07.551
for a robot's existence.

00:23:07.619 --> 00:23:09.052
When they've achieved
that purpose...

00:23:09.121 --> 00:23:12.056
humans and robots
will live in harmony.

00:23:12.124 --> 00:23:14.183
That's what we believe in.

00:23:14.259 --> 00:23:18.628
There are many different brands
on Mars, aren't there?

00:23:18.697 --> 00:23:21.723
When terraforming
on Mars began...

00:23:21.800 --> 00:23:26.965
robots were used for
environmental testing and labor.

00:23:29.174 --> 00:23:32.302
Well, I'm amazed
that we've come this far.

00:23:33.746 --> 00:23:37.182
In spite of our progress,
people are still afraid...

00:23:37.249 --> 00:23:39.217
and they still misunderstand
the robots.

00:23:39.284 --> 00:23:44.085
Our vision may not be understood
by consumers yet.

00:23:59.872 --> 00:24:02.898
We want our jobs back!

00:24:13.419 --> 00:24:15.478
Well, uh...

00:24:15.554 --> 00:24:16.646
excuse me.

00:24:16.722 --> 00:24:18.155
Why not?

00:24:18.223 --> 00:24:22.489
I'm very sorry,
but I cannot allow you to see...

00:24:22.561 --> 00:24:25.689
He doesn't remember
the name Armitage at all?

00:24:25.764 --> 00:24:28.699
Asakura said
he's never heard of you.

00:24:28.767 --> 00:24:29.756
What?

00:24:29.835 --> 00:24:31.826
Don't mess with me,
you little bitch!

00:24:31.904 --> 00:24:35.203
Please stop, or I'll call
the security gadget.

00:24:37.876 --> 00:24:40.572
I guess it's useless
talking to a robot.

00:24:42.214 --> 00:24:44.842
Excuse us.

00:24:44.917 --> 00:24:49.377
Let me go!
I have business here!

00:24:49.455 --> 00:24:51.821
Put me... put me down!

00:24:53.492 --> 00:24:54.652
Come on!

00:24:54.726 --> 00:24:56.990
Put me down right now!

00:25:00.666 --> 00:25:03.692
What were you trying to
accomplish back in there?

00:25:06.839 --> 00:25:09.808
If you park here,
your car might get trashed.

00:25:12.911 --> 00:25:15.402
So... now what's next?

00:25:17.115 --> 00:25:19.208
Immigration
seems a likely place.

00:25:19.284 --> 00:25:20.717
I already went there...

00:25:20.786 --> 00:25:24.347
and I couldn't find
our guy on the list.

00:25:27.659 --> 00:25:30.594
I doubt we'll find
any records of him...

00:25:30.662 --> 00:25:32.994
'cause 37% of the population
isn't registered here.

00:25:34.933 --> 00:25:40.064
What the hell were you trying to
find out at Conception company?

00:25:40.138 --> 00:25:42.072
That's private.

00:25:42.140 --> 00:25:45.075
By the way, I've already
checked about the Thirds.

00:25:45.143 --> 00:25:46.576
The company set...

00:25:46.645 --> 00:25:48.078
the original standards
for the Seconds...

00:25:48.146 --> 00:25:49.738
but I still pity them...

00:25:49.815 --> 00:25:56.050
because Hu-Gite passed 'em up,
and it killed their aspirations.

00:25:56.121 --> 00:26:00.023
Say, does this car have
reclining seats?

00:26:00.092 --> 00:26:01.957
What?

00:26:02.027 --> 00:26:04.552
Stop flying solo.

00:26:05.764 --> 00:26:07.322
We're partners, aren't we?

00:26:12.204 --> 00:26:13.330
Hey, Ross.

00:26:13.405 --> 00:26:15.566
As your partner,
can I make a suggestion?

00:26:15.641 --> 00:26:16.573
What?

00:26:16.642 --> 00:26:19.110
I'm starving.

00:26:19.177 --> 00:26:21.077
All right.

00:27:10.829 --> 00:27:12.262
Here. For you, Ross.

00:27:12.331 --> 00:27:13.263
What's this?

00:27:13.332 --> 00:27:16.267
I thought you were hungry.

00:27:16.335 --> 00:27:18.200
Oh, well...

00:27:20.806 --> 00:27:22.933
Lively town.

00:27:23.008 --> 00:27:26.136
They're getting carried away
remodeling their Seconds.

00:27:26.211 --> 00:27:30.807
There's no way humans and robots
are gonna get along together.

00:27:30.882 --> 00:27:31.974
Robots are, after all...

00:27:32.050 --> 00:27:33.745
You are no different.

00:27:34.886 --> 00:27:37.320
You and that guy are the same.

00:27:37.389 --> 00:27:39.880
That guy?

00:27:39.958 --> 00:27:43.724
It seems you have something
against robots.

00:27:43.795 --> 00:27:49.825
I just don't want to hang out
with non-humans.

00:27:49.901 --> 00:27:52.836
I'm sick and tired
of cyborgs and robots...

00:27:52.904 --> 00:27:54.872
that just seem to copy us.

00:28:48.794 --> 00:28:52.230
You're 'vestigating
her identity.

00:28:52.297 --> 00:28:54.128
Izzat right, Detective?

00:28:54.199 --> 00:28:57.396
Yes. It's my job.

00:28:57.469 --> 00:28:59.733
I wonder what Kelly's
fans would think...

00:28:59.805 --> 00:29:01.739
if they saw the real her.

00:29:01.807 --> 00:29:05.971
She was the most human girl
I knew...

00:29:06.044 --> 00:29:09.207
so sensitive and in touch.

00:29:09.281 --> 00:29:12.079
She didn't listen
to her manager...

00:29:12.150 --> 00:29:14.345
'cause she always
did things her way.

00:29:16.521 --> 00:29:18.955
How could she be a robot?

00:29:19.024 --> 00:29:21.288
Hah! It's too funny.

00:29:25.997 --> 00:29:27.931
I don't believe it!

00:29:27.999 --> 00:29:29.899
She's a real girl!

00:29:29.968 --> 00:29:32.402
I know how you feel...

00:29:32.471 --> 00:29:37.340
but did you recall anything
unusual about her?

00:29:38.844 --> 00:29:40.038
Excuse me.

00:29:40.112 --> 00:29:42.672
Please!
Tell me she's still alive!

00:29:42.748 --> 00:29:45.080
Please find her!

00:29:45.150 --> 00:29:47.141
She couldn't possibly
be a robot!

00:29:47.219 --> 00:29:50.154
No robot could sing
with that same passion...

00:29:50.222 --> 00:29:52.281
or make a guitar weep
like she did!

00:29:53.959 --> 00:29:55.859
Armitage!

00:29:58.230 --> 00:30:00.562
Kelly's dead.

00:30:00.632 --> 00:30:02.065
Get real!

00:30:03.201 --> 00:30:04.361
Hey!

00:30:06.404 --> 00:30:09.339
Hey, Armitage. Wait up!

00:30:09.407 --> 00:30:12.001
Let's get outta here.

00:30:12.077 --> 00:30:14.011
Your conduct
was hardly professional.

00:30:14.079 --> 00:30:15.512
What do you mean?

00:30:15.580 --> 00:30:18.014
Do you sympathize
with that guy?

00:30:18.083 --> 00:30:19.482
That cold-blooded bastard?

00:30:23.722 --> 00:30:26.156
Once he learned Kelly
was a robot...

00:30:26.224 --> 00:30:29.660
he started whining,
"That's not the Kelly I knew!"

00:30:32.097 --> 00:30:34.531
All of Kelly's talents
and all her efforts...

00:30:34.599 --> 00:30:36.396
were inside that machine!

00:30:36.468 --> 00:30:39.369
Are you...

00:30:39.437 --> 00:30:40.904
What is it?

00:30:45.310 --> 00:30:47.141
By any chance...

00:30:53.018 --> 00:30:54.076
Sylibus.

00:30:54.152 --> 00:30:57.417
Listen, I'm receiving
a weird mail transmission.

00:30:57.489 --> 00:30:58.956
Is Armitage with you?

00:31:00.091 --> 00:31:02.821
No, she's not here.

00:31:02.894 --> 00:31:06.660
It's coming in now,
so I'll transmit it to you.

00:31:06.731 --> 00:31:09.427
Log it and show it
to Armitage right away.

00:31:10.769 --> 00:31:13.704
I told you, it's an officer
named Armitage.

00:31:13.772 --> 00:31:16.206
We are looking for her
right now, ma'am.

00:31:16.274 --> 00:31:17.707
Help me, please!

00:31:17.776 --> 00:31:19.903
I'm a Third!

00:31:19.978 --> 00:31:21.536
What's your name?

00:31:23.949 --> 00:31:25.940
Manning...

00:31:26.017 --> 00:31:27.985
Jessica Manning.

00:31:28.053 --> 00:31:29.816
O.K. Listen,
I'm keeping a list...

00:31:29.888 --> 00:31:32.789
of all the Thirds
from Pluto.

00:31:32.858 --> 00:31:35.292
We need protection!

00:31:35.360 --> 00:31:38.295
I can't go outside
because of the protests.

00:31:38.363 --> 00:31:41.799
And the man on TV
has just sent me some mail.

00:31:41.867 --> 00:31:43.562
I know he's nearby!
Hurry up!

00:31:56.147 --> 00:31:57.239
Who are you?

00:32:30.882 --> 00:32:32.816
TV piracy is a felony, pal.

00:32:32.884 --> 00:32:35.819
You could get eight years
of hard labor in prison.

00:32:35.887 --> 00:32:37.821
Who the hell are you?

00:32:37.889 --> 00:32:39.584
D'anclaude.

00:32:41.192 --> 00:32:42.124
My name.

00:32:42.193 --> 00:32:45.560
Is D'anclaude your name?

00:32:45.630 --> 00:32:50.090
There are other things
to concern yourself with.

00:32:50.168 --> 00:32:51.601
The problem is...

00:32:55.607 --> 00:32:59.236
robots are disguising
themselves as humans.

00:32:59.311 --> 00:33:01.040
Am I wrong?

00:33:01.112 --> 00:33:02.545
If I don't kill them...

00:33:02.614 --> 00:33:04.172
you would
have been fooled by...

00:33:04.249 --> 00:33:08.015
sickening things
called Thirds.

00:33:08.086 --> 00:33:10.020
I've just found another one.

00:33:10.088 --> 00:33:12.989
This is Jessica Manning...

00:33:13.058 --> 00:33:13.990
Shit!

00:33:14.059 --> 00:33:16.823
A snobbish,
bourgeois artist.

00:33:16.895 --> 00:33:18.624
But she's a robot.

00:33:18.697 --> 00:33:20.824
What should we do about her?

00:33:23.969 --> 00:33:24.936
What should we do?

00:34:00.338 --> 00:34:02.533
Are you one
of Manning's relatives?

00:34:02.607 --> 00:34:03.539
Jessica!

00:34:03.608 --> 00:34:07.305
Save her, please!

00:34:14.185 --> 00:34:16.745
All right. Just wait here.

00:34:23.962 --> 00:34:27.261
Let me through! Police!
Let me through!

00:34:49.220 --> 00:34:50.653
It's them!

00:34:50.722 --> 00:34:52.019
The list of Thirds!

00:34:56.628 --> 00:34:58.459
Yes... and then?

00:34:58.530 --> 00:34:59.758
Ah! No, wait!

00:35:14.913 --> 00:35:17.245
Is that you, Jessica?

00:35:38.703 --> 00:35:39.670
Wait!

00:36:34.926 --> 00:36:37.258
Up we go!

00:36:37.328 --> 00:36:39.762
If you've come to confess
your sins...

00:36:39.831 --> 00:36:41.264
it's too late, my son.

00:36:41.332 --> 00:36:44.267
There's no room for religion
on Mars anymore.

00:36:44.335 --> 00:36:47.270
If you like,
I'll listen to you.

00:36:47.338 --> 00:36:49.932
You say a cyborg
killed your partner?

00:36:50.008 --> 00:36:52.636
Then you should join me.

00:36:53.811 --> 00:36:56.245
The more human a robot looks...

00:36:56.314 --> 00:36:59.306
the more excitement I feel
killing the damn thing.

00:37:10.061 --> 00:37:12.552
Well, shall we start?

00:37:38.756 --> 00:37:42.715
I'm just exterminating
illegal robots!

00:37:47.699 --> 00:37:51.465
Why do you make me
the bad guy and chase me?

00:37:57.642 --> 00:37:59.542
Shit! Not again!

00:38:08.086 --> 00:38:10.987
Please, stop chasing me, man.

00:38:11.055 --> 00:38:16.118
There are lots of Thirds
I have to destroy.

00:38:30.074 --> 00:38:32.099
Hey, what's this leg?

00:38:37.949 --> 00:38:40.383
This has gotta be
the irony of ironies.

00:38:40.451 --> 00:38:43.386
A fake leg?

00:38:43.454 --> 00:38:48.687
You wanna replace your body and
be a stinking cyborg yourself?

00:39:06.411 --> 00:39:07.708
What's that?

00:39:18.122 --> 00:39:19.953
Armitage!

00:39:23.328 --> 00:39:25.796
A bell to mourn the dead.

00:39:25.863 --> 00:39:30.857
Tell your friend, man,
there is no God on Mars anymore.

00:39:37.375 --> 00:39:38.535
D'anclaude!

00:39:38.609 --> 00:39:41.840
Let me tell you why
I cannot forgive your crimes...

00:39:41.913 --> 00:39:45.314
why I am on the robots' side...

00:39:45.383 --> 00:39:47.783
how I can justify
the existence of the Thirds.

00:39:47.852 --> 00:39:49.444
Let me tell you.

00:39:51.089 --> 00:39:53.557
Because of my blood...

00:39:53.624 --> 00:39:56.184
because of my destiny...

00:39:56.260 --> 00:39:57.249
What?

00:40:01.332 --> 00:40:03.266
Because...

00:40:03.334 --> 00:40:06.269
I'm also a Third.

00:40:06.337 --> 00:40:07.634
What did you just say?

00:40:07.705 --> 00:40:09.502
Armitage...

00:40:10.541 --> 00:40:12.475
You can't be!

00:40:12.543 --> 00:40:14.568
Your name
wasn't even on my list!

00:40:40.605 --> 00:40:42.038
Let me show you...

00:40:42.106 --> 00:40:45.405
the evidence of the Third,
the power of the Third!

00:41:00.992 --> 00:41:03.654
Here, bitch! You like it hot?

00:41:28.386 --> 00:41:30.251
Monster...

00:41:36.461 --> 00:41:39.055
Yeah, that's right.
I'm a monster.

00:41:39.130 --> 00:41:41.064
What are you gonna do?

00:41:41.132 --> 00:41:43.066
You gonna destroy me
or what?

00:41:43.134 --> 00:41:46.228
They blame us for recession
and social problems.

00:41:46.304 --> 00:41:49.569
If humans don't want us,
why did they make us?

00:41:55.613 --> 00:41:59.606
Stop! Don't kill him!

00:41:59.684 --> 00:42:02.152
Just cuff him, Armitage.

00:42:02.220 --> 00:42:04.347
You are a police officer
first.

00:42:06.624 --> 00:42:09.058
Robots aren't
the enemies of humans.

00:42:09.126 --> 00:42:10.957
The opposite is also true.

00:42:11.028 --> 00:42:12.256
Am I wrong?

00:42:30.114 --> 00:42:32.048
No! Don't look at me!

00:42:42.059 --> 00:42:44.323
Look at my body.

00:42:44.395 --> 00:42:47.592
I'm not a human.

00:42:47.665 --> 00:42:50.600
Even though I'm beaten
up like this...

00:42:50.668 --> 00:42:53.296
I still can stand... and talk.

00:42:55.706 --> 00:42:58.140
And I don't even feel pain!!

00:42:58.209 --> 00:42:59.972
Armitage!

00:43:16.093 --> 00:43:18.425
Armitage!

00:43:27.905 --> 00:43:30.339
Come on, kid.
Don't short out on me.

00:43:30.408 --> 00:43:32.535
Get up, now. Hey! Hey!

00:43:38.716 --> 00:43:40.047
Armitage...

00:43:40.117 --> 00:43:41.550
Hey, get up.

00:43:41.619 --> 00:43:43.610
Open your eyes.

00:43:51.062 --> 00:43:53.030
Ah. Thank God.

00:43:53.097 --> 00:43:54.758
Thank God?

00:43:54.832 --> 00:43:56.493
For what?

00:43:57.568 --> 00:43:59.729
What the hell are you
thankful for?

00:44:02.740 --> 00:44:04.674
You don't understand
anything at all!

00:44:04.742 --> 00:44:08.200
You couldn't possibly
imagine how I feel!!

00:44:08.279 --> 00:44:09.246
Hey.

00:44:12.283 --> 00:44:14.080
Goodbye.

00:47:05.089 --> 00:47:09.651
I'm a Third,
but I have feelings...

00:47:09.727 --> 00:47:10.989
memories, too.

00:47:11.061 --> 00:47:12.323
But where are the other Thirds?

00:47:12.396 --> 00:47:14.091
Please answer me!

00:47:15.733 --> 00:47:19.692
Armitage III, Episode 2,
"Flesh & Stone."

00:47:19.770 --> 00:47:22.000
Ross, don't follow me.
